$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of a solution of
tri(2-methyl-2-propanethioxy)aluminum hydride (LTBSA) in THF An
oven-dried, 250-mL, round-bottomed flask with a side arm, equipped with a
condenser leading to a mercury bubbler was flushed dry nitrogen and
maintained under a static pressure of nitrogen. To this flask was charged
100 mL of a solution of LiAlH4 in THF (2.0 M, 200 mmol), and followed by
dropwise addition of 55.8 g of 2-methyl-2-propanethiol (620 mmol) via a
double-ended needle with vigorous stirring at 25°C until the hydrogen
evolution was completed. The resulting clear solution was standardized by
hydrolyzing an aliquot with 3 N HCl-THF mixture to be 1.2 M, and kept
under nitrogen at 0°C. The THF solution of LTBSA was characterized by a
characteristic absorption in the IR at around 1,640 cm-1 (νAl-H) and by a
broad single at δ 129 ppm in the 27Al NMR relative to Al(H2O)6 3+.
Hexanal: Yield: 29%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in-situ generated reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reaction of lithium tris(tert-butylthiolato)hydridoaluminate with
selected organic compounds containing representative functional groups
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cha, Jin Soon; Yu, Se Jin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Inclusion Phenomena and Macrocyclic Chemistry (2009), 65(1-2),
7-13

