$DATUM (+)-[2S,(S)R]-3-(p-Methoxybenzyloxy)-1-(p-tolylsulfinyl)-2-propanol (3a):
A solution of β-ketosulfoxide 2 (5.8 g, 17.6 mmol, 1 equiv) in anhydrous
THF (30 mL) under an argon atmosphere was treated with a solution of
DIBALH (1.0 M in heptanes) (21.2 mL, 21.2 mmol, 1.2 equiv) at -78 °C.
Stirring was prolonged until the starting product could no longer be
detected by TLC (3 h) and the reaction was quenched with a saturated
aqueous solution of ammonium chloride (60 mL) at 0 °C. Then, a saturated
solution of sodium potassium tartrate (150 mL) in a mixture of AcOEt:H2O
(1:1), was added. Magnetic stirring was kept until aluminium salts were
solved (2-6 h), and the organic layer was separated by extraction with
AcOEt (3 x 75 mL), dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo
to give a yellowish oil. The crude obtained was purified by
chromatography on silicagel (Hexane:AcOEt, 1:3) to give a white solid
which crystallized in a mixture of Hexane:CH2Cl2 provided 3a in a 98 %
yield as white needles:
(+)-[2S,(S)R]-3-(p-Methoxybenzyloxy)-1-(p-tolylsulfinyl)-2-propanol (3a),
yield 98 % m.p. 50-52 °C (Hexane:CH2Cl2); [α]D 20 +146 (c 1.0, CHCl3),
Lit. for enantiomer 1 [α]D 20 -151 (c 1.0, CHCl3); 1H-NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 2.40 (s, 3H, p-TolSO), 2.71-3.08 (AB part of ABX system, JAB =
13.5, JAX = 9.7, JBX = 2.4 Hz, Δν = 81.2 Hz, 2H, -CH2- SOpTol), 3.37-3.53
(AB part of A´B´X system, JA´B´ = 9.8, JA´X = 5.6, JB´X = 4.8 Hz, Δν =
27.7 Hz, 2H, -CH2-CHOH), 3.79 (s, 3H, CH3O-Ar); 4.31-4.41 (m, X part of
both ABX systems, 1H, -CH-OH), 4.43 (AB system, JAB = 11.3 Hz, 2H,
Ar-CH2-O-), 6.85 (d, Jd = 8.7 Hz, 2H, Ar-OCH3), 7.19 (d, Jd = 8.7 Hz, 2H,
Ar-OCH3), 7.32 (d, Jd = 7.9 Hz, 2H, p-TolSO), 7.51 (d, Jd = 8.3 Hz, 2H,
p-TolSO); 13C-NMR (75 MHz) δ 21.3, 55.2, 59.5, 65.8, 72.8, 73.0, 113.8
(2CH, Ar-OCH3), 123.9 (2CH, p-TolSO), 129.4 (2CH, Ar-OCH3), 129.7, 130.0
(2CH, p-TolSO), 139.9, 141.5, 159.3.
