$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (+)-[2R,(S)R]-3-(p-Methoxybenzyloxy)-1-(p-tolylsulfinyl)-2-propanol (3b):
From a room temperature stirred solution of β-ketosulfoxide 2 (2.9 g, 8.7
mmol, 1 equiv) and Yb(OTf)3 (5.8 g, 9.6 mmol, 1.1 equiv) in anhydrous THF
(40 mL) (2 h), a solution of DIBALH (1.0 M in THF) (12.7 mL, 12.7 mmol,
1.5 equiv) was added at -78 °C. The reaction progress is controlled by
TLC and once it is finished (6 h) the reaction was quenched with a
saturated aqueous solution of ammonium chloride (20 mL) at 0 °C. Then, a
saturated solution of sodium potassium tartrate (150 mL) in a mixture of
AcOEt:H2O (1:1) was added. Magnetic stirring was kept until aluminium
salts were solved (2-6 h), and the organic layer was separated by
extraction with AcOEt (3 x 50 mL), dried over MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated in vacuo to give a yellowish oil. The crude was studied by
NMR to establish a 92:8 diastereomeric ratio between two alcohols (96 %
yield). After chromatography on silicagel (Hexane:AcOEt, 1:1) the major
diastereomer was enriched to de 88%. White needles:
(+)-[2R,(S)R]-3-(p-Methoxybenzyloxy)-1-(p-tolylsulfinyl)-2-propanol (3b),
yield 96 % m.p. 96-98 °C (Hexane: CH2Cl2); [α]D 20 +101 (c 1.1, CHCl3);
1H-NMR (300 MHz) (only the signals corresponding to 3b) δ 2.41 (s, 3H,
p-TolSO), 2.89-3.05 (AB part of ABX system, JAB = 13.3, JAX = 8.1, JBX =
3.8 Hz, Δν = 25.9 Hz, 2H, -CH2-SOpTol), 3.43-3.62 (AB part of A´B´X
system, JA´B´ = 9.9, JA´X = 5.9, JB´X = 5.3 Hz, Δν = 34.5 Hz, 2H,
-CH2-CHOH), 3.56 (sbr,1H, -OH), 3.79 (s, 3H, CH3O-Ar), 4.25-4.36 (m, X
part of both ABX systems, 1H, -CH-OH), 4.44 (s, 2H, Ar-CH2-O-), 6.86 (d,
Jd = 8.7 Hz, 2H, Ar-OCH3), 7.22 (d, Jd = 8.7 Hz, 2H, Ar-OCH3), 7.32 (d,
Jd = 7.9 Hz, 2H, p-TolSO), 7.54 (d, Jd = 8.3 Hz, 2H, p-TolSO); 13C-NMR
(75 MHz) δ 21.3, 55.2, 60.0, 67.5, 72.6, 73.2, 113.8 (2CH, Ar-OCH3),
124.0 (2CH, p-TolSO), 129.4 (2CH, Ar-OCH3), 129.7, 130.0 (2CH, p- TolSO),
140.5, 141.8, 159.4; MS (m/z) 76 (14), 77 (11), 121 (100), 83 (20), 85
(13), 91 (16), 121 (100), 137 (28), 138 (18), 181 (41), 334 (M+, 0.03);
HRMS (EI) Calcd for C18H22O4S 334.1239, Found 334.1229; Anal. Calcd for
C18H22O4S C, 64.64; H, 6.63; S, 9.59, Found C, 64.67; H, 6.66; S, 9.16.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimized on reducing agent (DIBALH better than LAH,
sodium borohydride, tetrabutylammonium borohydride), catalyst (Yb(OTf)3
better than zinc chloride, bromide or iodide)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
