$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(4,6,7-Trimethoxy-1-tosylindol-3-yl)ethane-1,2-diol (9) To a solution
of compound 8 (2.60 g, 5.64 mmol) in a mixture of anhydrous ether (100
mL) and anhydrous THF (50 mL) at - 5°C, LiAlH4 (0.749 g, 19.7 mmol) was
added in small portions. The reaction mixture was allowed to warm up to
10°C, then stirred at that temperature for 2 h. TLC examination (ethyl
acetate/hexanes, 3:1) indicated the completion of the reaction. The
reaction mixture was then cooled back to 0°C and quenched by slow
addition of an aqueous solution of saturated Na2SO4. The inorganic solids
were filtered off, and the residue was washed with dichloromethane (75
mL). The combined filtrate was concentrated under vacuum to obtain the
crude residue. The crude residue was dissolved in dichloromethane (100
mL) and washed with water (3 x 50 mL) and brine (1 x 50 mL). The organic
layer was dried over Na2SO4 and filtered, and the solvent was removed
under vacuum to obtain the crude product, which was purified by column
chromatography over silica gel (15 x 3 cm) using ethyl acetate/ hexanes
(3: 1) to afford the pure product 9 as a white solid (1.92 g, 81%).
1-(4,6,7-Trimethoxy-1-tosylindol-3-yl)ethane-1,2-diol (9), yield 1.92 g,
81%. mp 109-110°C; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 2.36 (s, 3H), 3.76 (s, 3H), 3.87 (s,
3H), 3.88 (d, 2H, J = 6.3 Hz), 3.94 (s, 3H), 5.01 (t, 1H, J = 6.3 Hz),
6041 (s, 1H), 7.23 (d, 2H, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.62 (s, 1H) and 7.75 (d, 2H, J =
8.1 Hz); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 21.5, 55.9, 56.8, 60.6, 6604, 68.7, 92.9,
114.6, 119.5, 124.1, 127.2 (2C), 129.5 (2C), 129.9, 131.2, 136.4, 144.2,
147.7, and 150.6; IR (CHCl3) 3416 cm-1; MS (ES+) m/z 404 (M - H2O + H).
Anal. calcd. for C20H23NO7S: C, 57.00; H, 5.50; N, 3.32. Found: C, 56.89;
H, 5.32; N, 3.26.
