$DATUM (1S,2R)-2-((4-methoxyphenyl)amino-1,2-diphenylethan-1-ol 25: To a 10 mL
flame-dried round bottom flask was added the amino ketone (S)-23s (0.0756
g, 0.24 mmol, 1 equiv, 95% ee) and 2 mL THF. The solution was cooled to
-78 °C in dry ice/acetone bath for 5 min under a N2 atmosphere and
lithium triethylborohydride (0.48 mL, 1M in THF, 0.48 mmol, 2 equiv.) was
added dropwise via a syringe. The resulting mixture was kept at -78 °C
for 15 min before being quenched with saturated NH4Cl solution. The
solution was then gradually warmed up to room temperature and extracted
with ether (5 mL x 3), dried over MgSO4, filtered through filter paper in
Büchner funnel and concentrated under rotary evaporation. The anti:syn
ratio was greater than 50:1 by 1H NMR analysis of the crude reaction
mixture. The product was purified by flash column chromatography on
silica gel with 8:1 to 4:1 hexanes:EtOAc as eluent. The product 25 as a
light yellow solid (80%, 0.0605 g, 0.19 mmol). mp = 115-116 °C (lit11
121-124 °C). The optical purity was determined to be 92% ee by Chiralcel
OD-H column, 95:5 Hexane:iPrOH, 1 mL/min flow rate, 220 nm, 19.3 min for
the minor peak and 23.7 min for the major peak. Spectral data for
(1S,2R)-25 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 2.51 (br s, 1H), 3.68 (s, 3H), 4.24
(br s, 1H), 4.61 (d, J = 4.5 Hz, 1H), 5.05 (d, J = 4.5 Hz, 1H), 6.50 (d,
J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 6.68 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 7.09-7.11 (m, 2H), 7.14-7.15
(m, 2H), 7.24-7.29 (m, 6H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ 55.65, 64.65,
77.10, 114.67, 115.50, 126.58, 127.57, 127.90, 127.94, 128.19, 128.28,
138.67, 140.00, 140.71, 152.43; [α]20 D = +50.7° (c = 1.0, CHCl3) on 90%
ee, [lit11 +27.9°, c = 1.0, CHCl3, on 93% ee]. The NMR data are in
agreement with those in the literature.11
