$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Sodium borohydride (0.019 g, 0.527 mg, 3 eq.) is added, at -78°C, to a
solution of ketone 25 (0.1 g; 0.175 mmol, 1 eq.) in MeOH (1 ml). The ice
bath is removed and the reaction is stirred, at room temperature for 24h.
The mixture is quenched with a saturated solution of sodium
hydrogenocarbonate. The aqueous phase is extracted with DCM and the
organic phase was dried over Na2SO4. After condensation the crude oil is
purified by column chromatography (EP/AcOEt= 3/1). 52.9 mg of a colorless
oil are obtained. Yield: 66%. 1H NMR (500 Mhz, CDCl3) δ: 5.71 (s, 1H);
5.29-5.50 (m, 2H); 3.75 (ddd, J= 1.8, 4.7, 13.2 Hz, 1H); 3.67 (m, 1H);
3.66 (s, 1H); 3.34 (dd, J= 2.1, 11.8 Hz); 3.26 (td, J= 6.4, 8.6 Hz, 1H);
3.19 (ddd, J= 2, 8.7, 10.1 Hz, 1H); 2.62 (d, J= 13.4 Hz, 1H); 2.41 (m,
1H); 2.15 (s, 3H); 2.04- 2.14 (m, 3H); 1.12 (d, J= 6.2 Hz, 3H); 0.95 (d,
J= 6.6 Hz, 3H); 0.87 (s, 9H); 0.10 (s, 3H); 0.07 (s, 3H).13C NMR (125
Mhz, CDCl3) δ: 167.0, 157.1; 134.2; 131.2; 117.0; 79.2; 75.5; 73.7; 71.0;
67.9; 50.7; 44.8; 43.1; 41.3; 27.9; 25.3; 20.2; 18.1; 16.6; -3.6; -4.3.
I.R. (cm-1): 3475, 2955, 2929, 2887, 2856, 1718, 1648, 117. M.S. (CI)
m/z: 455.2 (M-, 20), 376.4 (35); 341.2 (100); 255.6 (37); 165.9 (33),
126.9 (35).
