$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,1'-di(1-hydroxyethyl)ferrocene (11). A solution of LiAlH4 (0.301 g,
7.54 mmol) in anhydrous THF (7 ml) was cooled to -78°C and 1,1'-
diacetylferrocene (3 g, 10.8 mmol) previously dissolved in THF (30 ml)
was added dropwise. After 1 h of stirring at rt the solution was cooled
again to-78°C and more LiAlH4 (110 mg, 2.90 mmol) was added. The reaction
mixture was stirred for 2 h at rt. After the reaction was complete, ethyl
acetate (2.7 ml) and water (1 ml) were added and the solution was
filtered washing de formed precipitate with diethyl ether. After
evaporation of the solvent, the residue was purified by recrystallization
in hexane to yield 11 (1.92 g, 65%). 1 H-NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3) δ/ppm 4.63
(quint, J= 6.2 Hz, 2 H, CH), 4.20 (m, 8 H, Cp), 3.57 (s, 2 H, OH), 1.42
(d, J= 6.2 Hz, 3 H, CH3), 1.40 (d, J= 6.2 Hz, 3 H, CH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM incremental addition of LiAlH4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Do Molecular Conductances Correlate with Electrochemical Rate Constants?
Experimental Insights
