$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reduction of Benzaldehyde; Typical Procedure:
To the freshly prepared reagent, dry n-hexane (10 ml) and then
benzaldehyde (106 mg, 1.0 mmol) are added under an atmosphere of
nitrogen. After stirring for 3 h at 25 °C (at the reflux temperature in
the cases of esters), the excess reagent is quenched with a saturated
aqueous solution of ammonium chloride (0.3 ml): the mixture is filtered
and the silica gel washed thoroughly with diethyl ether (10 ml). The
filtrate and the washings are combined and the solvent is removed.
Without further purification. Product: 2i, Yield: 62%, Substrate: 1i,
Amounts used 1: 1.0 mmol, LiAlH4: 3.0 mmol, SiO2: 1.0 g, Solvent:
n-hexane (10). b.p. Found: 44°C/0.01 torr, reported: 44°C/0.01 torr.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Lithium aluminum hydride reduction in nonpolar solvents: use of silica
gel as an effective catalyst
